  "notes": "USAGE:\nUsed both as a noun and as a する verb ({占有|せんゆう}する = to occupy, to possess exclusively). In legal contexts, it refers to having physical control over property. In business, {占有|せんゆう}{率|りつ} (occupancy rate / market share) is a key metric.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {占有|せんゆう}{率|りつ} (market share, occupancy rate)\n- {占有|せんゆう}{権|けん} (right of possession)\n- {占有|せんゆう}する (to occupy, to possess exclusively)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {独占|どくせん}: monopoly — complete control of a market or resource, stronger than {占有|せんゆう}",
